# Ohm standard library — single-gate logic (std.logic)
#
# "Little logic" single-gate parts in the SOT-23-5 pinouts standardized
# across the 74xx1G families (TI, Nexperia, Diodes, onsemi second-source the
# same pad order). Honesty (N3): concrete pads only for that shared family
# convention; level shifters have no cross-vendor standard and stay a
# TEMPLATE comment block. NO ratings invented — declare your part's limits
# at instantiation, e.g. SingleGate_SOT23_5(vmax=5.5V).

# Single 2-input gate, SOT-23-5. The 74xx1G two-input convention shared by
# 74LVC1G00 / 1G08 / 1G32 / 1G86 (and AHC1G/AUP1G/AUC1G equivalents):
#   1=A  2=B  3=GND  4=Y  5=VCC
# The gate FUNCTION (NAND/AND/OR/XOR) is part-specific — set mpn= on your
# instance; the pad order is what this block standardizes.
use std.kinds

component SingleGate_SOT23_5(LogicGate):   # kind-checked: out/vcc/gnd present (A/B inputs extra)
    package = generate(SOT23, pins=5)
    designator_prefix = "U"
    pin A:   role=input, pad=1
    pin B:   role=input, pad=2
    pin GND: role=ground, pad=3, is=gnd
    pin Y:   role=output, pad=4, is=out
    pin VCC: role=power_in, pad=5, is=vcc

# Single inverter, SOT-23-5. The 74xx1G one-input convention used by
# 74LVC1G04 (inverter) and 74LVC1G14 (Schmitt inverter), 1G17 buffer etc.:
#   1=NC  2=A  3=GND  4=Y  5=VCC
# Convention chosen: TI/Nexperia 1G04 SOT-23-5 (DBV) pin order, in which
# pad 1 is not connected. VERIFY against your exact datasheet before layout
# — a few single-input parts repurpose pad 1.
component Inverter_SOT23_5(Buffer):   # kind-checked: inp + inherited out/vcc/gnd (NC unbound)
    package = generate(SOT23, pins=5)
    designator_prefix = "U"
    pin NC:  role=nc, pad=1
    pin A:   role=input, pad=2, is=inp
    pin GND: role=ground, pad=3, is=gnd
    pin Y:   role=output, pad=4, is=out
    pin VCC: role=power_in, pad=5, is=vcc

# TEMPLATE (adapt to your datasheet): single-bit level shifter.
# No cross-vendor pad standard: 74LVC1T45 (directed, DIR pin) and TXB0101
# (auto-direction, OE pin) differ, multi-bit parts differ again. Canonical
# 74LVC1T45 SOT-23-6 roster for reference:
#   1=VCCA  2=GND  3=A  4=B  5=DIR  6=VCCB
#
# component LevelShifter_MYPART:
#     package = generate(SOT23, pins=6)
#     designator_prefix = "U"
#     mpn = "..."
#     pin VCCA: role=power_in, pad=1
#     pin GND:  role=ground, pad=2
#     pin A:    role=bidirectional, pad=3
#     pin B:    role=bidirectional, pad=4
#     pin DIR:  role=input, pad=5
#     pin VCCB: role=power_in, pad=6
